CAVEAT. These numbers are on SIMULATED pedestrians, from CARLA.
The labels are exact, which is the point, but the people are not
real: they walk on a navmesh, they are lit by a game engine, and
they never do any of the things a gesture head exists to catch.
This is a measurement of the pipeline on synthetic video with
ground-truth labels. It is NOT accuracy on real pedestrians, and
it should never be quoted as one. The run that would mean that
is --source jaad with a pose cache, and it needs the clips.
